// Price levels for the world. The game is set in the present day (every car through the catalog year,
// smartphones, EVs) but the cost of living is the mid-1990s United States: houses and cars are cheap
// relative to wages, so a help-desk technician at ~$15/hr lives comfortably.
// vehicles: multiplier on the catalog's 2010s-baseline prices (0.55 puts a family sedan around $16k).
// housing:  multiplier on city home prices, which are already authored in 1995 dollars.
// goods:    multiplier for prices computed from modern baselines (paint jobs, some services).
// wages:    multiplier on career pay, which careers.json already lists in 1995 dollars.
{
  "era": "Present day, 1995 prices",
  "calendarYear": 2026,
  "catalogYear": 2026,
  "vehicles": 0.55,
  "housing": 1.0,
  "goods": 0.55,
  "wages": 1.0
}
